  "created": "2024-07-05T20:16:38.988Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I am trying to use TeleportTo to change where the player is looking. If I set the teleportRot Quaternion parameter of this function to Identity (all 0s), the player's vertical look angle is retained after the teleport.\n\nIf the player was looking straight upwards, I should expect the angle they are looking at to be completely neutral after the teleport, but this is not the case.\n\nI have tried setting the Teleport orientation to AlignPlayerWithSpawnPoint and AlignRoomWithSpawnPoint but neither of these two seem to change anything.\n\nI am unsure if this behaviour is an intentional aspect of this function, but it is stopping me from implementing a system in my VRChat world that I would like. This is my first bug report so forgive me if the explanation of the problem is poor.",
